From 139085c1aa36c772bd6ac7c3956f0cdd6e3a57f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Certe Kim <18364439+CerteKim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:08:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: round the DSC active width up like the DSI host
 does

drm_mode_to_intf_timing_params() truncates the compression-ratio scaled
active width for DSI DSC panels:

	timing->width = timing->width * bpp / (bpc * 3);

The DSI host derives the hdisplay it programs for the very same line with
DIV_ROUND_UP() in dsi_timing_setup().  Whenever the compressed line does
not divide evenly, the two sides disagree by one pclk unit and the DPU
interface is programmed one unit short of what the DSI transmits.  On the
CSOT PNC357DB1-4 (1600 px wide, 8 bpc, 8 bpp, single DSC slice) that is
533 against 534, so the DSI FIFO underflows, no valid frame reaches the
panel and the screen stays black although the backlight is on.

Use DIV_ROUND_UP() here as the 6.18 bring-up tree did, so both sides
program the same width.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
index ba810f26ea30..e1007aeb9f93 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
@@ -134,8 +134,9 @@ static void drm_mode_to_intf_timing_params(
 		 * TODO: replace drm_dsc_get_bpp_int with logic to handle
 		 * fractional part if there is fraction
 		 */
-		timing->width = timing->width * drm_dsc_get_bpp_int(dsc) /
-				(dsc->bits_per_component * 3);
+		timing->width = DIV_ROUND_UP(timing->width *
+				drm_dsc_get_bpp_int(dsc),
+				dsc->bits_per_component * 3);
 		timing->xres = timing->width;
 		timing->dce_bytes_per_line = msm_dsc_get_bytes_per_line(dsc);
 	}
